{"name":"Eiffel Tower","hex":"#998e83","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Eiffel Tower","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An iron tower built in 1889 on the Champ de Mars beside the Seine River in Paris; a global icon of France and one of the most recognizable structures in the world."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spit roast with the two penetrating partners holding hands."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Eiffel_Tower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eiffel Tower","blocks":[{"text":"The Eiffel Tower is a lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France. It is named after the engineer Gustave Eiffel, whose company designed and built the tower from 1887 to 1889."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/ba/Eiffel_Tower_logo.svg/330px-Eiffel_Tower_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eiffel_Tower"},{"title":"Eiffel Tower (Six Flags)","blocks":[{"text":"The two Eiffel Towers in Six Flags parks—one at Kings Dominion and one at Kings Island—are replicas of the Eiffel Tower in Paris, France. They each opened with their respective park, the first at Kings Island in 1972 and the second at Kings Dominion in 1975."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kings_Dominion_Eiffel_Tower.jpg/330px-Kings_Dominion_Eiffel_Tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eiffel_Tower_(Six_Flags)"},{"title":"Tower","blocks":[{"text":"A tower is a tall structure, taller than it is wide, often by a significant factor. Towers are distinguished from masts by their lack of guy-wires and are therefore, along with tall buildings, self-supporting structures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Tokyo_Sky_Tree_2012.JPG/330px-Tokyo_Sky_Tree_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",